  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Akhilesh Baghel vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 19 January, 2023 Author: Atul Sreedharan Bench: Atul Sreedharan",
    "facts": "But for offence under Section 420 of IPC the other offences are bailable in nature.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicants submits that the applicants have maliciously been implicated in this case and that even if their actions constituted irregularities, the same would be offences or misdemeanors under the Food Safety and Standards Act. He further says that under the Special Act, their actions would only be liable to fine and not even imprisonment. Learned counsel for the State while opposing the application for bail submits that upon inspection by the Food Inspector, lot of raw material which allegedly bore fungus and was emanating a bad smell and certain other articles used for manufacture of sweets were kept there, the cartons were also not lebelled etc. He further submits that in the case diary, there is no report of the Food Analyst which would disclose that the articles seized from the applicants are unfit for human consumption or toxic in nature.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicants submits that the applicants have maliciously been implicated in this case and that even if their actions constituted irregularities, the same would be offences or misdemeanors under the Food Safety and Standards Act. He further says that under the Special Act, their actions would only be liable to fine and not even imprisonment. Learned counsel for the State while opposing the application for bail submits that upon inspection by the Food Inspector, lot of raw material which allegedly bore fungus and was emanating a bad smell and certain other articles used for manufacture of sweets were kept there, the cartons were also not lebelled etc. He further submits that in the case diary, there is no report of the Food Analyst which would disclose that the articles seized from the applicants are unfit for human consumption or toxic in nature.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
